WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:06.729
One of the funnier, lighter moments in Game
of Thrones Season 6 is Tormund’s adorable

00:00:06.729 --> 00:00:09.370
crush on Brienne of Tarth.

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:14.059
Brienne doesn’t reciprocate, sadly, but
in the books there are hints of another woman

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:17.090
Tormund may have a secret romance with.

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:22.120
You know how Daenerys is famous for having
a lot of titles – she’s Daenerys Targaryen,

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:26.370
“First of Her Name, Queen of Meereen, Queen
of the Andals and the Rhoynar and the First

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:30.480
Men, Lord of the Seven Kingdoms, Protector
of the Realm, Khaleesi of the Great Grass

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.960
Sea”, Stormborn, the Unburnt, Mother of
Dragons , myhsa and “Breaker of Chains”

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:39.160
. Well, in the books, Tormund, too, has many
names.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.149
They call him “Tormund Giantsbane, Tall-talker,
Horn-blower, and Breaker of Ice”.

00:00:44.149 --> 00:00:49.129
“Tormund Thunderfist, Husband to Bears,
the Mead-king of Ruddy Hall, Speaker to Gods

00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:53.920
and Father of Hosts” . Tormund’s quite
a different character in the books compared

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:59.760
to the show – he’s more funny, always
joking, drinking, telling tall stories.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:05.070
And one tale he tells explains one of his
titles – “Husband to Bears”.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:10.290
The story goes that one cold winter’s night,
Tormund was drinking alone, when he decided

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.840
to go visit a woman he knew nearby.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.290
He went out, got a bit lost, but eventually
found the woman, and, though she fought him,

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:21.430
got her out of her furs and had sex with her.

00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:26.300
When Tormund woke up the next morning, he
found his body ripped and torn, half his penis

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.470
bitten off, and “a she-bear’s pelt”
lying beside him.

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:36.080
Turns out he had sex with a bear, and supposedly
a “bald bear” is later seen in the woods,

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.970
with “the queerest pair o’ cubs behind
her” . This story obviously isn’t literally

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:47.090
true – Tormund’s a notorious “bag of
wind and lies” , called “Tall-talker”

00:01:47.090 --> 00:01:52.170
after all – but there are hints that the
story might be loosely based in truth, possibly

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:59.430
revealing a secret relationship between Tormund
and Lady Maege Mormont.

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:03.890
House Mormont is a northern family based on
Bear Island, up near the Wall.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:08.920
They’re led by Jeor Mormont ‘til he joins
the Night’s Watch, then by Jorah Mormont

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:14.180
‘til he flees Westeros after selling slaves
– he ends up serving with Daenerys.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:19.700
So now the leader of House Mormont is Lady
Maege, who’s called “the She-Bear” . So

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.079
the theory here is that Tormund’s story
of “a she-bear” is not really about an

00:02:24.079 --> 00:02:29.239
actual bear – it’s about “the She-Bear”
of Bear Island, Maege Mormont.

00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:30.799
And there are hints supporting this.

00:02:30.799 --> 00:02:36.180
Tormund describes both the woman he knows
nearby and the she-bear as having a “temper”.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.140
Maege is described as “stubborn”, “willful”,
and “short-tempered”.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:45.310
Maege is also described as a “stout” and
“strong” “warrior” which fits with

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:50.489
Tormund’s descriptions of “a fine strong
woman”, and of the fighting she-bear.

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:55.740
It is a bit confusing whether Maege is more
the woman Tormund knows or the She-Bear in

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.950
this story, maybe it’s a bit of both.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.659
But the point is that Tormund’s she-bear
story does seem to have connections with the

00:03:02.659 --> 00:03:06.459
She-Bear of Bear Island, Lady Maege.

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:10.959
And there’s more, cause Lady Maege has five
daughters, though no one seems to know who

00:03:10.959 --> 00:03:16.420
the father is, or if Maege has a husband . Maege’s
daughter Alysane, who herself has a couple

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.529
of kids, also apparently has no husband.

00:03:19.529 --> 00:03:22.389
She says “Mormont women are skinchangers.

00:03:22.389 --> 00:03:25.659
We turn into bears and find mates in the woods.

00:03:25.659 --> 00:03:31.599
Everyone knows” . This, again, is probably
not literally true, but it supports the idea

00:03:31.599 --> 00:03:39.159
that Mormont women are metaphorically she-bears,
out in the woods mating with men like Tormund.

00:03:39.159 --> 00:03:41.019
This also could make logistical sense.

00:03:41.019 --> 00:03:44.269
Bear Island is very close to the wildling
lands beyond the Wall.

00:03:44.269 --> 00:03:48.670
Maege says that it’s because of the threat
of being “carried off” by ironmen or by

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:53.989
wildlings that Mormont women need to be warriors
. So it’d make sense for Tormund and Maege

00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:56.980
to have met during a wildling raid on Bear
Island.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:04:02.029
In Tormund’s story he claims to have carried
the “she-bear” back to his home, which,

00:04:02.029 --> 00:04:07.969
in wildling culture, constitutes a marriage
– thus making Tormund “Husband” to “the

00:04:07.969 --> 00:04:08.969
She-Bear”.

00:04:08.969 --> 00:04:14.120
Of course none of this sounds terribly consensual
on Maege’s part, what with the talk of carrying

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.030
off, and the fighting she-bear.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:20.001
But there’s reason to believe that this
relationship between Tormund and Maege, if

00:04:20.001 --> 00:04:26.270
it exists, may be consensual and positive
and ongoing, partly because of the positive

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:31.250
way Alysane talks about the Mormont she-bears
mating in the woods, and partly because the

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:36.650
way Tormund talks about the woman who lives
nearby does sound like an ongoing relationship,

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:43.440
but also because an ongoing consensual relationship
could better explain Maege’s daughters.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.360
Tormund says that the “she-bear” bears
him “cubs” – children – maybe these

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:53.280
are Maege daughters, those of the mysterious
unknown father.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:58.170
Tormund also mentions “sons”, which might
mean that Maege is the mother of some of Tormund’s

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:03.940
four sons . It sounds almost as though Maege
chooses to keep her five daughters, but gives

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:09.330
her sons to be raised by Tormund beyond the
Wall – though it’s hard to imagine how

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:11.699
Maege could do all this secretly.

00:05:11.699 --> 00:05:16.510
This is a lot of kids to come from a secret
relationship across the Bay of Ice, so maybe

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:20.460
only some of the kids are the children of
Tormund with Maege.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.669
But even if it’s only some, that’s very
significant.

00:05:24.669 --> 00:05:30.740
Maege and Tormund may not be the first wildling-non-wildling
relationship in the series – there’s Jon

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:36.680
and Ygritte, and Gilly and Sam – but Maege
Mormont is the Lady of Bear Island, a ruler

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:41.470
in the north – if her kids have free folk
blood in ’em, if lil’ Lyanna Mormont is

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:46.340
half wildling, that could really impact the
attitudes of people in the north, who of course

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:48.539
mostly hate wildlings.

00:05:48.539 --> 00:05:53.379
Bridging this gap between the wildlings and
northmen is becoming more important with white

00:05:53.379 --> 00:05:58.599
walkers on the way, and any connection between
Tormund and Maege could maybe help with this

00:05:58.599 --> 00:06:00.050
alliance.

00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:05.420
The hatred between northmen and wildlings
also adds a layer of tragedy to a relationship

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:10.460
between Tormund and Maege – they’re separated
by sides that have been enemies for centuries,

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:14.160
star-crossed like Romeo and Juliet with the
Montagues and Capulets.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:18.800
And of course by Dance, Tormund and Maege
are split further apart – Tormund is at

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:24.070
Castle Black, while Maege is way down in the
Neck, possibly involved in a northern conspiracy.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.740
The lovers are now so far apart.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:31.439
“Would that I could find her again”, Tormund
says.

00:06:31.439 --> 00:06:36.200
So look there’s no strong evidence for a
relationship between Tormund and Maege.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:41.110
Tormund’s story may be just a story, and
Maege’s daughters may’ve been fathered

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:43.690
by some common man on Bear Island or something.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:44.690
Fine.

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:49.530
But the hints and connections with “strong”
bad-tempered she-bears are there, and the

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:55.050
logistics and timing could work, so it is
at least fairly possible that “Husband to

00:06:55.050 --> 00:07:01.250
Bears” Tormund and “the She-Bear” Maege
Mormont get together on one cold winter’s

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:02.610
night.

